@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch17ch18-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch17ch18-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 17 and 18"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.11.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch17ch18-lineage/1.11.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch17ch18_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.11.0 (2026-11-11): Change request, execution record. Both repeated stories replaced in new draft versions; the revised drafts re-compared with chapters 1-16."@en .

ex:TK7_Uniq_ReplaceCh17 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "03-materials/ch17/DRAFT_ch17_v1_0_2.md: story 3 (Office Open XML standard, December 2006 and 2008, already told in chapter 14) replaced by 'Charles Simonyi, Richard Brodie and the Computer History Museum', 25 March 2014 (sources read 2026-11-11: Computer History Museum blog and press release of 25 March 2014, The Register of the same date). v1.0.1 and v1.0.0 stay on disk unchanged." .
ex:TK7_Uniq_ReplaceCh18 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "03-materials/ch18/DRAFT_ch18_v1_0_1.md: story 3 (JSON origin, Crockford and Morningstar, April 2001, already told in chapters 7 and 10) replaced by 'Jesse James Garrett, co-founder of Adaptive Path', 18 February 2005 (sources read 2026-11-11: heise.de 20-years article, a copy of Garrett's essay with its 13 March 2005 questions and answers, O'Reilly Ajax Design Patterns chapter 1). v1.0.0 stays on disk unchanged." .
ex:TK7_Uniq_Review backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Re-compared the 12 stories by people, event, date and source with the live story scripts of chapters 1-16 (Adobe, Warnock, pypdf, Brian Jones, RFC 4180, Fortran, SGML, billion laughs, Computer History Museum, Adaptive Path: no earlier chapter). Result: no unconfirmed repeat. One borderline case named, not decided: chapter 18 story 5 (ElementTree added in Python 2.5, 19 September 2006, and json in 2.6) reads the same 'What's New in Python 2.5' release page that chapter 16's SQLite story uses; the subject, people and module differ. Lower bound only: a comparison by words cannot prove two stories differ." .
ex:ST7_StoryUniqueness backlog:hasState backlog:Done .
ex:ST7_ApprovalGate backlog:hasState backlog:Ready ;
    rdfs:comment "Unblocked: both drafts now carry the replaced stories (ch17 v1.0.2, ch18 v1.0.1) and are sent to the owner."@en .

ex:Obs1_Obj7_StoriesNotRepeated a backlog:MetricObservation ; backlog:observationForMetric ex:Metric_Obj7_StoriesNotRepeated ;
    backlog:observedValue 0 ; backlog:observedAt "2026-11-11T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:comment "Measured: ch17 story 3 and ch18 story 3 replaced; re-comparison finds none; one borderline case (ch18 story 5 and ch16, same Python 2.5 release page) named for the owner."@en .
